\\n/// this worker can produce a model reply without threetched chat/generate CLI.\\n/// Dispatch target: `op_llm::chat::ChatManager` (our stack), not\\n/// `threetched.stateless-generate` and not `tched_router.Chat`.\\nconst OUR_GENERATE_CALLMETHOD: &str =\\n    \\\"PluginService.CallMethod{plugin_id=\\\\\\\"large_language_model\\\\\\\",method=\\\\\\\"stream_generate\\\\\\\"}\\\";\",\r\nreports/tched-routing-audit-20261024/crates/op-chat-responder/judgments.md:23:    \"src/main.rs:308-351\": \"process_turn observes provider/model using observe_selection, then calls our_stack_generate with generation.prompt and response_mode. Ok(frame) checks type done, exact provider/model match and bounded nonempty response before commit_response. Err(error) builds automatic generation deferred reason with OUR_GENERATE_CALLMETHOD and calls refuse. refuse at265-278 invokes chat_response.cannot_perform through call_response. [Source summary, not verbatim.]\"\r\nreports/tched-context-audit-20261024/crates/op-chat-responder/findings.md:16:`our_stack_generate` is an explicit `bail!` stub. Its own comments require a combiner to seal, grant, guest-mount, and route the CallMethod before replacing the stub. On this source path, a generation error is converted to `chat_response.cannot_perform`; the source does not establish that admitted turns can currently generate a reply. This is a broader integration gap, not a tched naming/context defect, and this single-crate audit provides no verified schema/grant/receiver contract to implement it safely. It was not changed.\r\nreports/tched-context-audit-20261024/crates/op-cozo-store/coverage.tsv:14:crates/op-cozo-store/src/chat_response_conversations.rs\t1116\tcomplete_through_EOF\t0\r\nreports/tched-context-audit-20261024/crates/op-grpc-bridge/coverage.tsv:41:crates/op-grpc-bridge/src/chat_response_dispatch.rs\t1076\tread\t1-1076 through EOF\tSequential inventory line 37\r\nreports/tched-context-audit-20261024/crates/op-grpc-bridge/coverage.tsv:42